  "scope": "WB button in Develop arms a direct eyedropper and reveals four original-pixel sample areas; RAW and RGB paths retain distinct semantics. Includes the existing uncommitted UI polish.",
  "implemented": [
    "Auto white balance arms a custom eyedropper cursor and requests native detail automatically; a valid click applies and saves once.",
    "One-row area choices 1x1, 3x3, 5x5 and 11x11 below the button; default 5x5; selection alone never edits the recipe.",
    "Escape or a second button click cancels picking. Photo, recipe, cache and panel changes invalidate the target; previous hover samples are never reused.",
    "Current native coordinates map back through RAW geometry, including crop and rotation. Invalid, incomplete, stale or provisional samples are rejected without saving.",
    "Experimental RAW uses the bounded native fitter for 1x1 and 3x3; existing CFA estimation is preserved for Auto, 5x5 and 11x11. Other RAW engines use the existing native fitter for all four areas.",
    "JPEG/PNG/TIFF expose the same interaction with relative RGB warmth/tint, retaining compatibility and sample-validity limits.",
    "Compact control spacing keeps exposure visible in a 550x360 logical inspector. Italian and English help and README usage updated."
  ],
